      "content": "- **Do not let him sleep it off.** The danger window is the next 24–48 hours, and a stroke can happen during sleep.\n- **There is no home monitoring plan that makes this safe.** Watching for symptoms only works after a doctor has evaluated him — not instead of one.\n- **The bill is a real concern, but a stroke costs far more** — financially and in every other way. Many hospitals have financial assistance or payment plans.\n- **If you truly won't go to the ER, call his doctor or a nurse line right now** — but understand they will almost certainly tell you to go to the ER.\n- **Go now if any of these appear:** face drooping, arm weakness, slurred speech, confusion, vision changes, severe headache, trouble walking.\n\nPlease take him in. That's the only safe answer here.",
